food is my absolute favorite way to  explore my heritage esopes son mis  favoritos hey everyone i'm diana and i'm  here with my mom  hola  and today we're making mexican sopas  mexican sopas are a traditional mexican  recipe they're basically a handmade  tortilla stacked with a bunch of  different toppings and they're really  delicious one of the most amazing things  for me is the way in which my mom is  able to just kind of fill out all the  measurements without actually measuring  every single ingredient for example when  it comes to making the dough my mom's  looking for a certain softness and  consistency and basically when she gets  to that elasticity with the dough she's  able to make the sockets  california chilies are not necessarily  really spicy especially when you scoop  out all the seeds from inside but they  bring out a really good flavor to the  coating of the soap  so when it comes to boiling the tomatoes  you want to look out for the skin of the  tomato to start peeling off and once  they're doing that it's time to turn  down the fire and pull them out the  tomato dressing is actually one of the  most simple types of dressings that you  could make the simplicity of it allows  the tomato flavors to really stand out  basically i grew up in mexico for a few  years while i was very young even though  i live in the u.s i am very much very  mexican my mom continues to instill in  us a lot of the traditions through food  or through our culture in general that  she grew up with and to some extent that  i grew up with i'm not the best cook but  my mom is and so i really like to take  tips from her but also be in the kitchen  with her and just kind of like seeing  all the crazy things that she does i  really value my heritage i think that it  has taught me so much not only about  food but about so many other traditions  i like my steak to be cut down to just  small square pieces and that's always  how my mom has done it it just makes it  easier to eat you want to make sure that  you allow your sopas to cool off before  you dip them in the hot sauce and start  frying them because if you don't let  them chill out for at least an hour the  heat will disintegrate the dough i  basically grew up eating sopas and a ton  of other classic mexican recipes soap is  for sure one of my all-time favorite i  may be biased but i think my mom makes  the best mexican sopas ever me gusta la  cosina mexicana porque loca  and now the best part about sopas is  that you could add as much toppings as  you like obviously i like to put as much  as possible  [Music]  oh yes  you
 

